    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Sell\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan concludes with an Underweight stance, and the technical evidence strongly supports trimming exposure. AAPL trades below every major moving average (10 EMA at $172.85, 50 SMA, 200 SMA), with MACD at -4.33 well below its signal line and a deeply negative histogram. The 20-day return of -9.22% and 60-day return of -11.51% confirm a sustained multi-week downtrend, not a one-day event. While the fundamental quality (AAA balance sheet, $30.6B quarterly capital return) and deeply oversold RSI at 27.98 argue against aggressive liquidation, the plan's disciplined conclusion is to reduce exposure to underweight. The realistic near-term risk-reward is roughly 1:1 (upside to 10 EMA ~2.3% vs downside to 52-week low ~2.9%, with no support below until $150), which does not justify holding a full position. I recommend trimming the position by ~15-25% to underweight, with a hard stop below the 52-week low at $164.08 and a re-entry trigger on reclaiming the 10 EMA at $172.85 on above-average volume.\n\n**Entry Price**: 168.89\n\n**Stop Loss**: 164.08\n\n**Position Sizing**: Trim to underweight (60-75% of benchmark weight); reduce existing position by 15-25%\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **SELL**",
